From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: drewano <drewano@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-msm: force runtime suspend before s2idle

Upstream sdhci_msm_runtime_suspend gates clocks immediately and relies on
pm_runtime autosuspend (200ms) to quiesce the SD slot. During s2idle
entry the autosuspend timer can race the system suspend path: the PM core
polls RPMh for AOSD/CXSD while the SD controller is still technically
runtime-active, and spurious SD IRQs (~30/s on Odin 2, armada#274)
repeatedly reset the timer so the controller never actually suspends.

Pocknix addresses this by carrying the full Qualcomm downstream
sdhci-msm driver (0210, ~6200 lines) which defers clock gating to a
delayed_work and flushes it synchronously in suspend_late(). Rather than
import the downstream driver, take the minimal PM-relevant idea: ensure
the SD controller is runtime-suspended before the system suspend path
proceeds.

This patch adds a suspend prepare callback that forces the controller
into runtime suspend if it is still active. Prepare runs after the
thermal core quiesces zones and before suspend callbacks, so autosuspend
state is stable. pm_runtime_suspend() respects the usage counter —
an SD rootfs with in-flight I/O leaves the controller active and returns
-EBUSY, which we treat as non-fatal (safe). Resume is via the existing
pm_runtime_force_resume in SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS.

References: armada#274 (mmc0 IRQ storm, 30 irq/s while
runtime_status=suspended), Pocknix 0210 analysis by hugare, follow-up
0212 (SDCC RCG floor ops revert). Already have 0204 tsens prepare — same
phase ordering.

Complements the dwc3 qcom PHY fix (0520) — together they address both
RPMh vote holders on SM8550 that block CX/AO collapse.
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
@@ -2934,6 +2934,36 @@ static int sdhci_msm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+static int __maybe_unused sdhci_msm_prepare(struct device *dev)
+{
+	/*
+	 * s2idle thermal: armada#274 shows mmc0 firing ~30 irq/s during
+	 * s2idle while reporting runtime_status=suspended. The autosuspend
+	 * timer can race system suspend and spurious IRQs reset it, so
+	 * the controller never truly gates. Prepare runs after the thermal
+	 * core quiesces zones and before suspend callbacks — force runtime
+	 * suspend if still active. Safe for SD rootfs: in-flight I/O holds
+	 * the PM usage counter and pm_runtime_suspend() returns -EBUSY.
+	 */
+	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(dev)) {
+		int ret = pm_runtime_suspend(dev);
+
+		if (ret == -EBUSY || ret == -EAGAIN) {
+			dev_dbg(dev, "prepare: controller busy, deferring suspend (%d)\n", ret);
+			return 0;
+		}
+		if (ret && ret != 1) {
+			/* 1 means already suspending; only warn on real errors */
+			dev_warn(dev, "prepare: runtime suspend failed %d\n", ret);
+		} else if (!ret || ret == 1) {
+			dev_dbg(dev, "prepare: forced runtime suspend before s2idle\n");
+		}
+	}
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct dev_pm_ops sdhci_msm_pm_ops = {
+	.prepare = sdhci_msm_prepare,
 	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(sdhci_msm_runtime_suspend, sdhci_msm_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
